<?xml version="1.0"?>
<config xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="urn:magento:framework:Module/etc/module.xsd">
    <module name="Spartrak_Catalog" setup_version="1.0.0">
        <sequence>
            <module name="Magento_Catalog"/>
            <module name="Magento_CatalogSearch"/>
            <!--
              Magento_Swatches: ViewModel\BrandNavigation reads the header
              mega-menu's brand logos from the per-option VISUAL SWATCH IMAGES
              an admin uploads against the `brand` attribute, using that
              module's own Helper\Data and Helper\Media. Declared so this
              module always loads after it.
            -->
            <module name="Magento_Swatches"/>
            <!--
              Magento_Eav: this module's two data patches use EavSetup to add
              the category hero attributes and the five specification filter
              attributes. Declared so both always run after EAV's own setup.
            -->
            <module name="Magento_Eav"/>
            <!--
              Magento_Store: AddSpecFilterAttributes resolves which store views
              are Arabic before writing their attribute labels.
            -->
            <module name="Magento_Store"/>
            <!--
              ===================================================================
              Spartrak_Homepage IS DELIBERATELY *NOT* SEQUENCED HERE.
              ===================================================================
              Adding it looks right — Block\Category\QuickSearch type-hints that
              module's ViewModel\CascadeOptions, and Block\Product\RelatedRail
              has long rendered its section/head.phtml — but it breaks the
              install outright:

                  Circular sequence reference from 'Spartrak_Homepage'
                  to 'Spartrak_Catalog'.

              Spartrak_Homepage already sequences AFTER this module, because
              every one of its product sections renders through
              Spartrak_Catalog::product/card.phtml. Declaring the reverse closes
              the loop, and Magento rejects a cyclic module graph.

              Not declaring it is correct rather than merely expedient. `sequence`
              orders LOAD-TIME MERGES — layout XML, di.xml, config, setup patches.
              Neither reference needs one: a constructor type-hint is resolved by
              the autoloader and DI at runtime, and a `Module::template.phtml` id
              is resolved by the view-file fallback at render time. Neither
              consults the sequence graph at all.

              What the shared code genuinely is, is a pair of leaf collaborators
              — one ViewModel and one presentational partial — with no layout, no
              section and no setup of their own. If either ever grows something
              that DOES need merge ordering, the fix is to move it into a third
              module both can sequence after, not to re-add this line.
            -->
        </sequence>
    </module>
</config>
